    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d298">

                <pb facs="0527" n="481" sameAs="frus:frus1914-20v02/pg481"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">710.11/203½</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">President Wilson to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-04-27">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">27 April, 1915</hi>
                        </date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Secretary</hi>: This seems to me
                        excellent.<anchor n="10" xml:id="d298-f1"/> I agree with you that it is wise
                    to be explicit and that it is well to put these views in writing, as you have
                    done.</p>
                <p>I think it would be wise, however, to state that the provisions as to territory
                    as you restate them in this letter are not definitively proposed (for we have
                    not yet shown them to Argentine and Brazil, upon whose cooperation we are
                    depending) but are formulated by way of suggestion of what we would be quite
                    willing to discuss, if in that form they commended themselves to the Chilean
                    government.</p>
                <p>Faithfully Yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>W. W.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d298-f1" n="10" xml:id="d298-f1-content">
                <p>Draft of letter to the Chilean Ambassador; for the letter as sent, see <hi
                        rendition="#italic">infra.</hi>
                </p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
